hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17741","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Aws ibn Abdullah Abu Muqatil al-Saluli narrated to me who said: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from his father Malik ibn Rabia, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, forgive those who shave. O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man among the people said: And those who shorten. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the third or on the fourth: And those who shorten. Then he said: And I that day was shaven-headed, so nothing would please me for the shaving of my head in exchange for red camels or a great prize."
